  "title": "Nana Asma'u",
  "summary": "Nana Asma'u, a daughter of the Sokoto Caliphate's founder Usman dan Fodio, was a poet and scholar with more than 60 surviving works, in Arabic, Fulfulde and Hausa. Around 1830 she created a cadre of women teachers, the jajis, who travelled to teach women in their homes. She died in 1864.",
